1
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:43,800
Weird.

2
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,240
Very weird.

3
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:50,320
Zheng Yu suddenly borrowed an outfit
from Fangli.

4
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,680
She's up to no good.

5
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:56,080
Did that ruse from this afternoon work?

6
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,880
They hit it off and are going on a date.

7
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:01,680
That proves Fangli is an expert at this.

8
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:05,720
What's wrong?

9
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,120
I chose the wrong outfit.

10
00:02:08,199 --> 00:02:09,759
That outfit today

11
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,560
didn't show my full potential.

12
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,240
I forgot to ask.

13
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:35,200
How did you two meet in the first place?

14
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:39,880
All of Xiaomian's customers
are students in his grade.

15
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:42,560
You're not in the same grade.
How did you meet?

16
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:46,320
I chose him at first glance
from a sea of people.

17
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,120
You chose him based on looks?

18
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:56,000
There's nothing interesting
about this ordinary face.

19
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,240
You called me good-looking.

20
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:00,880
Twice.

21
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,720
It was a jab at you
for pretending to be cool.

22
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:08,560
Couldn't you even tell?

23
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,640
When I arrived at the school today,

24
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:15,480
I think someone said,

25
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,880
"Although he's good-looking,

26
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:19,720
from my observations,

27
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,400
dating him would be quite boring."

28
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,080
Shut up!

29
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:25,000
Dating?

30
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,960
How old are you?

31
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:29,440
The point is the latter part.

32
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,960
"Boring."

33
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:31,920
Get it?

34
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,080
Should you even consider it?

35
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,920
You shut up too.

36
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,200
Are you laughing?

37
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:42,840
Does being my rumored boyfriend

38
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:43,920
make you happy?

39
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,720
Who ordered beer?

40
00:04:06,480 --> 00:04:07,640
I did.

41
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,720
You're out of control.

42
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,080
You said Ms. Zheng
was going to be naughty.

43
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:15,720
She can't leave now.

44
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:19,399
Besides,

45
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,880
alcohol reveals the truth.

46
00:04:20,959 --> 00:04:23,480
Since you two saved my life today,

47
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,640
I've done what I can.

48
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:28,040
I have something to say.

49
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:39,480
Chen Yanzhou.

50
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,720
Your outfit today

51
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:47,920
looks sharp.

52
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:48,480
Your sister really can't hold her alcohol.

53
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:51,480
I'll take her back to campus first.

54
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,160
- Where are you going?
- With my sister.

55
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:58,000
And then? You'll make
my cousin take you home?

56
00:05:58,600 --> 00:05:59,800
No.

57
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:04,800
How are you two getting home?

58
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,680
- He said he'll take me.
- I didn't.

59
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,120
You did.

60
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,800
I heard it.

61
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:14,080
Message me when you get home.

62
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,000
And you.

63
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:17,640
You memorized my number.
Don't forget to message me.

64
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,400
Be careful.

65
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:37,440
Jiang Mian!

66
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,760
Jiang Mian.

67
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,440
Jiang Mian.

68
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:42,960
Jiang Mian.

69
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,040
Can you stop saying my name?

70
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:47,840
<i>Ms. Zheng's mom is surnamed Jiang.</i>

71
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:50,800
<i>But Jiang Mian wasn't born</i>
<i>with his mother's surname.</i>

72
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:53,360
<i>It's because he was adopted by his uncle.</i>

73
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,760
Then what do I call you, if not your name?

74
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:57,800
Smarty?

75
00:06:57,880 --> 00:06:59,120
Hottie?

76
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,040
Mian?

77
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:02,760
Or…

78
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,200
Xiaomian?

79
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:11,160
Xiaomian, why are you walking so fast?
Do you know where I live?

80
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:14,120
I never agreed to see you home.

81
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:16,880
I wouldn't trust you to.

82
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:19,200
After all, there isn't an adult at home.

83
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:22,080
I would be helpless against you
if you made a move on me.

84
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:24,880
Stop playing the victim.

85
00:07:25,680 --> 00:07:27,600
Because we're the same.

86
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:29,320
My mom

87
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,520
also can't come to school.

88
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,080
And my dad has passed away too.

89
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,480
"Too"?

90
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:41,680
Didn't you tell the teacher
that your dad died long ago?

91
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:45,520
Yes, right, he's not here.

92
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:48,200
You lied?

93
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:52,680
A dad who cheated and remarried
is no different from being dead.

94
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,320
Lead the way.

95
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:13,000
We missed the doors closing
by ten minutes.

96
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:18,480
Chen Yanzhou, stand straighter.

97
00:08:19,640 --> 00:08:21,160
You're so handsome today.

98
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,480
Don't hunch over.

99
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:26,320
You're drunk.

100
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:29,080
I'm not drunk.

101
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:35,080
Stand straighter.

102
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:56,240
Am I standing straighter now?

103
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:01,680
This is good for your spine.

104
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:07,080
Since I'm so obedient today,

105
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:08,520
can you lend me your phone?

106
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,040
Why do you want it?

107
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:24,440
The doors are closed.

108
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:28,200
I'll ask your roommates
to ask the dorm manager to open the door.

109
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:30,360
We can't let the dorm manager

110
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:33,520
see you drunk and escorted back by a boy.

111
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:37,840
No way.

112
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,200
If the dorm manager opens the door,

113
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,440
I'll have points deducted.

114
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,720
I have to get my prize money.

115
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:47,880
I have to make a lot,
a lot, a lot of money.

116
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,080
That won't do.

117
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:52,720
Then I'll take you…

118
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:54,360
to a hotel?

119
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,680
Do you have your ID?

120
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:03,600
Chen Yanzhou,

121
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:05,680
I can sleep on the street.

122
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:06,600
I…

123
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,000
I'll find a nice spot.

124
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:09,280
A nice spot. Here.

125
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:19,920
There's another place. Want to go?

126
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,200
Then let's go.

127
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,280
I can't walk anymore.

128
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:00,400
Why

129
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:02,400
are you looking at me?

130
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,560
Now you're quiet.

131
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,520
Chen Yanzhou.

132
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:15,280
Why have you been mad at me
for the past few days?

133
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:17,720
I haven't been.

134
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,520
You have.

135
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,520
You weren't like this before.

136
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,360
Tell me.

137
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:25,480
Tell me the reason

138
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,640
so I'll know how to sweet-talk you.

139
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:29,880
Sweet-talk me?

140
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:33,960
Sweet-talk you.

141
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:41,200
Yesterday, you went out
for lunch with Duan Shengyang.

142
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:44,560
What were you talking so happily about?

143
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,800
Shoot, I can't tell you.

144
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,680
Someone said she wanted to sweet-talk me.

145
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,760
I guess she was just kidding.

146
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,680
No.

147
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:56,320
Actually, that meal

148
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,720
wasn't enjoyable for me at all.

149
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:02,280
Liar. I saw you.

150
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,040
It's true.

151
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:06,120
Fine.

152
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:07,880
Then tell me.

153
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:10,120
How did Duan Shengyang make you unhappy?

154
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,760
It doesn't have to do with him.

155
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,200
It's your fault.

156
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,160
Me?

157
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:20,600
Because that meal

158
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:23,080
made me realize something
I didn't know before.

159
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:24,920
What?

160
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:27,600
I realized

161
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:29,640
that because of you,

162
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:31,600
I started to have expectations.

163
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,680
Expectations?

164
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:40,680
The expectation

165
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,560
that I, too, can have a future.

166
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:45,560
A wonderful future.

167
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:49,560
So shouldn't I blame you?

168
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,480
I'm not even angry with you.

169
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,480
But you're angry with me.

170
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:04,760
Zheng Yu.

171
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,840
You…

172
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,440
Lift your head first.

173
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:19,840
Zheng Yu.

174
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,920
Why do you look so serious?

175
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:42,800
Tell me.

176
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:44,680
How should I sweet-talk you

177
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:46,760
to make you smile?

178
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,160
I don't know.

179
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:52,680
Why don't you figure it out?

180
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:46,840
Zheng Yu, are you awake?

181
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:48,960
Can I come in?

182
00:15:56,120 --> 00:15:58,720
What's wrong with your neck?

183
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:01,200
Nothing.

184
00:16:01,280 --> 00:16:02,360
I must have slept wrong.

185
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:06,440
Last night, you--

186
00:16:06,520 --> 00:16:08,240
I drank too much last night.

187
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,080
I only remember Gao Xing
mentioning a rumored boyfriend.

188
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,520
That was hilarious.

189
00:16:14,320 --> 00:16:17,960
I… And then I don't remember much.

190
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:21,400
Right.

191
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:25,000
Where did you get that perfume
on your desk?

192
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,320
I saw it on your Moments and bought it.

193
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:35,080
So the buyer who chatted with me

194
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:36,120
was you.

195
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:45,960
Speaking of which, I have a complaint.

196
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,440
Your perfume
doesn't match the description.

197
00:16:49,640 --> 00:16:51,800
I specified that it had a flaw.

198
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,600
Is the scratch too obvious?

199
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,040
Why don't you…

200
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:02,200
This isn't how you described the scent.

201
00:17:19,839 --> 00:17:21,800
You have to inhale to smell it.

202
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:32,640
I told you.

203
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,680
I found the description online.

204
00:17:34,760 --> 00:17:36,680
I didn't know it would be so off.

205
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,280
Tell me how you want to settle this.

206
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,560
Have a meal with me.
Consider it compensation.

207
00:17:57,200 --> 00:18:00,880
Seller, this isn't the right attitude
for solving issues.

208
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:09,280
Do your parents know

209
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,960
that I stayed overnight?

210
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:13,360
If I walk out like this,

211
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,960
won't it be a bit awkward?

212
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:19,360
Why don't I wait for them to leave

213
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,560
before I come out?

214
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:25,480
What if my parents stay in all day?

215
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:27,640
Will you camp out in this room?

216
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,920
- Dad! Mom!
- Don't.

217
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,360
No one is here.

218
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:46,240
They've gone to my grandma's house
for a few days.

219
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:55,800
By the way, there are new toiletries
in the bathroom.

220
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,320
I'll wait for you downstairs.

221
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:06,760
Is it bad?

222
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:14,120
I know a method.

223
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,840
Try it.

224
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,480
This acupoint here is called
the Stiff Neck acupoint.

225
00:19:20,560 --> 00:19:22,360
Massage it for a minute or two.

226
00:19:23,800 --> 00:19:24,640
Turn your neck.

227
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:30,600
No.

228
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:33,120
Turn your head to the side that is stiff.

229
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:39,400
Why is the door open?

230
00:19:39,480 --> 00:19:40,320
Right.

231
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:49,440
Mr. and Mrs. Chen.

232
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:51,120
Dad, Mom.

233
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:58,120
I think I'm fine now.

234
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:01,080
Sir, ma'am,

235
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,320
I have to go now.

236
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,960
Bye.

237
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,800
Stay for a meal, Ms. Xiaozheng.

238
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:11,680
Look, I bought so many groceries.

239
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:14,440
No, thank you. I…

240
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:16,160
You helped fix my phone.

241
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:19,280
If you leave without eating,
I will feel bad.

242
00:20:19,360 --> 00:20:20,480
Let's do that.

243
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:28,240
Then I'll go help.

244
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:49,280
- This--
- Dad.

245
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:52,440
Why are you two back so early?

246
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:57,840
You know your grandma's temper.

247
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:00,400
Your mom and I
couldn't stand it after one night.

248
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:03,160
We left quickly after breakfast.

249
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,200
Oh, right.

250
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:11,040
These are freshly-picked mangoes.

251
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,960
They're not in stores
at this time of year.

252
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:16,680
Pack some for her to take home.

253
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:18,680
Okay.

254
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,000
Ma'am, these are washed.

255
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:28,360
What else can I help with?

256
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,280
Whip the eggs for me.

257
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:42,200
What's wrong?

258
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,680
Do you not like to eat eggs?

259
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:45,640
It's not that.

260
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:47,680
I just remembered something.

261
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,520
I learned only recently

262
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:52,600
that some people are allergic to eggs.

263
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:55,960
Are there people who are allergic to eggs?

264
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,760
Especially people
who have been seriously ill.

265
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,320
They may seem to have recovered,

266
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,720
but their bodies have weakened immunity

267
00:22:05,800 --> 00:22:07,360
and develop new allergies.

268
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:11,320
Then they should be careful.

269
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:15,560
After a serious illness, you never know

270
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:17,800
what long-term effects there might be.

271
00:22:25,760 --> 00:22:26,640
Here.

272
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:36,240
Last time, when I came here to drop off
the mock exam, I ate this here.

273
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:38,120
It tastes very special,

274
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,800
so it has been on my mind.

275
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,000
Is that so?

276
00:22:41,080 --> 00:22:42,360
Yes.

277
00:22:42,440 --> 00:22:44,960
A simple dish like this

278
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:47,280
really tests a chef's skills.

279
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,480
You sure like to brag.

280
00:22:49,560 --> 00:22:53,080
Xiaozheng, if you like it,
come over when you're free.

281
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:55,000
My wife is often at home.

282
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:56,760
It's just another place setting.

283
00:22:57,360 --> 00:22:59,000
I'm often not at home.

284
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:05,320
I mean

285
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:07,400
that our volunteer group

286
00:23:07,480 --> 00:23:08,760
has been very busy lately.

287
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,600
I'm often not at home, so…

288
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:15,960
Today's situation won't happen again.

289
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:22,560
Mom, she missed her dorm curfew yesterday,
so she stayed the night.

290
00:23:23,680 --> 00:23:24,960
It's not what you think.

291
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,840
She even stayed over?

292
00:23:52,800 --> 00:23:54,840
Don't mind what my parents said.

293
00:23:54,920 --> 00:23:56,960
We didn't have many options yesterday.

294
00:23:58,560 --> 00:23:59,840
Do you remember what you--

295
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:02,360
Things ended very late yesterday.

296
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:03,800
I must've been locked out.

297
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:07,640
I'm already very grateful
that you let me stay over.

298
00:24:08,960 --> 00:24:11,920
That's easy for you to say.
You've forgotten what you did.

299
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:19,080
Your parents seem very sweet together.

300
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:22,080
When we left, your dad even told me

301
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:24,080
that your mom loves to eat mangoes.

302
00:24:24,160 --> 00:24:28,400
But the juice gets all over her hands,
so she doesn't want to bother.

303
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:31,000
He always cuts them up for her.

304
00:24:32,560 --> 00:24:34,240
Yes, they are very close.

305
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:42,600
I cut up some mango.

306
00:24:42,680 --> 00:24:44,160
Try it.

307
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:50,320
They're far away by now.

308
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:52,920
Still looking?

309
00:24:53,960 --> 00:24:55,600
I just realized today.

310
00:24:55,680 --> 00:24:58,800
Even Yanzhou is old enough to date now.

311
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:00,360
Time sure flies.

312
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:04,000
Dating? What dating?

313
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:05,640
Far from it.

314
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:07,840
From what I see, your son's romance

315
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:10,360
is like these mangoes
that can't be sold yet.

316
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:12,000
Astringent.

317
00:25:12,080 --> 00:25:13,600
It's not ripe yet.

318
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:28,080
It's only 8:00 a.m. Am I seeing things?

319
00:25:31,720 --> 00:25:34,800
No, you aren't.
I plan to turn over a new leaf.

320
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:36,640
Didn't you say

321
00:25:36,720 --> 00:25:40,160
to get rid of those ridiculous thoughts
and work properly?

322
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Hey, don't look at me like that.

323
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:48,040
I'm serious. I even made preparations.

324
00:25:48,720 --> 00:25:49,560
Like what?

325
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:55,920
Vitamins.

326
00:25:56,000 --> 00:25:57,720
Liver support tablets.

327
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,520
Fast-acting heart-soothing pills.

328
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:02,520
Agarose. No, not this.

329
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:04,840
There's more.

330
00:26:06,080 --> 00:26:07,840
No, don't be impatient.

331
00:26:07,920 --> 00:26:10,000
There's more. Come.

332
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:13,000
Over here.

333
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:20,640
I'm surprised.

334
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:22,520
You're good at drawing.

335
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:25,480
Skills honed in the zoology lab class.

336
00:26:26,360 --> 00:26:27,600
What do you think?

337
00:26:29,440 --> 00:26:30,320
I have a question.

338
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:31,920
Shoot.

339
00:26:32,000 --> 00:26:32,960
Why

340
00:26:33,040 --> 00:26:34,480
are you in the middle?

341
00:26:36,200 --> 00:26:37,440
I have an announcement.

342
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:40,720
The boss's birthday party is
next Sunday evening.

343
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:42,080
I'll send you the address.

344
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:44,160
Midway through dinner,

345
00:26:44,240 --> 00:26:45,960
will he check on our progress?

346
00:26:46,040 --> 00:26:47,560
I'll pretend to be drunk.

347
00:26:47,640 --> 00:26:49,320
- I'm not done yet.
- Zero progress.

348
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,600
- Zheng Yu.
- Don't ask me.

349
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,080
And there's this.

350
00:27:04,280 --> 00:27:05,880
A birthday gift?

351
00:27:05,960 --> 00:27:07,960
Yes. We discussed it.

352
00:27:08,040 --> 00:27:10,800
One from the PhD students.

353
00:27:10,880 --> 00:27:12,440
One from the master's students.

354
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,560
Do you guys also…?

355
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:18,760
It doesn't have to be expensive.
He won't accept it then.

356
00:27:18,840 --> 00:27:21,640
It's been like that every year.
Just a small token.

357
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:23,480
I might not be free on Sunday.

358
00:27:24,520 --> 00:27:27,160
It won't take long. It's just dinner.

359
00:27:27,240 --> 00:27:29,600
Think of it as a group meeting.

360
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,240
If you're worried about the gift,

361
00:27:34,320 --> 00:27:37,480
when you're free, we can get one together
since I need one too.

362
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:40,080
Forget it.

363
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,200
This is our…

364
00:27:43,560 --> 00:27:46,560
This is our lab's
first team-building activity.

365
00:27:50,080 --> 00:27:53,000
I think you should go along with…

366
00:27:57,360 --> 00:27:59,960
I think you should go
along with everyone else.

367
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:01,560
We'll see.

368
00:28:07,320 --> 00:28:09,840
Okay, tell me if you need anything.

369
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:23,800
I thought coffee
wasn't good for your health.

370
00:28:25,560 --> 00:28:26,800
Who says it's for me?

371
00:28:28,400 --> 00:28:29,680
Buckle up.

372
00:28:29,760 --> 00:28:31,400
Bi Dezheng is serious.

373
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,960
What are you doing here?

374
00:29:06,040 --> 00:29:07,520
You've been standing here a while.

375
00:29:08,640 --> 00:29:10,160
Admiring the artwork.

376
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:14,120
A culture medium?

377
00:29:14,960 --> 00:29:16,840
What did you draw?

378
00:29:22,760 --> 00:29:24,080
You.

379
00:29:30,320 --> 00:29:32,640
My drawing skills
are not worse than Bi Dezheng's.

380
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:35,560
Do you have to compete in this too?

381
00:29:40,640 --> 00:29:42,720
When I had a stiff neck,

382
00:29:42,800 --> 00:29:44,360
did I look like this?

383
00:29:46,720 --> 00:29:48,040
That's not it.

384
00:29:50,920 --> 00:29:52,360
You really don't remember?

385
00:29:59,400 --> 00:30:01,760
Who says I can't remember?
I know it by heart!

386
00:30:13,720 --> 00:30:16,280
Sorry. I had a dream.

387
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:19,680
If you keep going, you will burn out.

388
00:30:20,800 --> 00:30:23,240
Let's call it a day. Let's go.

389
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:35,400
The lights don't work.

390
00:30:36,440 --> 00:30:39,360
Do the lights not work,
or is something haunting us?

391
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:41,120
What?

392
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:44,800
I left my phone charging cable
in the lab drawer.

393
00:30:45,840 --> 00:30:47,440
You scared me to death.

394
00:30:47,520 --> 00:30:50,000
Why didn't I ever notice
this hallway was so dark?

395
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:53,560
Maybe because you were never
the last one to leave.

396
00:30:56,200 --> 00:30:57,880
Wait for me.

397
00:31:15,160 --> 00:31:16,440
Why did you pull me back?

398
00:31:35,080 --> 00:31:38,120
You're also scared
but embarrassed to admit it. I get it.

399
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:43,320
Yes, I'm scared. Scared to death.

400
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,040
Then let's band together.

401
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,920
I have a mission for you.

402
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:50,280
Escort me safely to the restroom.

403
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:53,160
I'm about to burst.

404
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:56,040
Slowly. Not too fast.

405
00:32:31,560 --> 00:32:33,600
Want to go buy a gift together on Sunday?

406
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:39,000
Aren't we supposed to
prepare a small gift?

407
00:32:40,360 --> 00:32:41,280
You heard?

408
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:44,680
Yes. It's like Shengyang said.

409
00:32:44,760 --> 00:32:47,160
No attendance and no gift
would be inappropriate.

410
00:32:48,760 --> 00:32:50,160
Besides,

411
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:51,320
I have to talk to you.

412
00:33:09,520 --> 00:33:10,920
Chen Yanzhou!

413
00:33:37,040 --> 00:33:39,280
What is this?

414
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:43,800
What do you mean?
I heard you in the restroom.

415
00:33:44,800 --> 00:33:48,120
I'm going to the boss's party too.
How can you leave me out?

416
00:33:48,720 --> 00:33:51,160
Team building is important,
don't you know that?

417
00:33:54,680 --> 00:33:57,720
You said you had to talk to me.
What is it?

418
00:34:00,320 --> 00:34:01,880
No rush. Let's shop first.

419
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:07,120
- Have you decided where to go?
- No.

420
00:34:07,720 --> 00:34:09,880
You're lucky I came, you know that?

421
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:12,159
You don't know the boss as well as I do.

422
00:34:12,800 --> 00:34:15,040
Our professor likes music.

423
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:17,040
He has a record collection at home.

424
00:34:29,280 --> 00:34:30,600
How is this one?

425
00:34:33,199 --> 00:34:34,199
I think it's great!

426
00:34:53,159 --> 00:34:55,760
With this cover,
even I would feel awkward giving it.

427
00:34:58,920 --> 00:35:00,560
Or we change our approach.

428
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:03,280
I heard our boss has a daughter
in kindergarten.

429
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:04,240
He dotes on her.

430
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:06,000
In my opinion,

431
00:35:06,080 --> 00:35:07,640
we could buy a stuffed animal.

432
00:35:08,400 --> 00:35:09,520
Let's go.

433
00:35:15,480 --> 00:35:16,760
Zheng Yu, do you think…

434
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,960
A gift that's not for children's eyes?

435
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:23,240
Do you think we'll ever graduate
from the lab then?

436
00:35:23,320 --> 00:35:25,520
Listen to me. Put it down.

437
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:31,560
Plan C is a set of books.

438
00:35:31,640 --> 00:35:34,480
It's unoriginal, but it's a safe bet.

439
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:45,160
What are you doing?
We said books. This way.

440
00:35:52,520 --> 00:35:55,320
None of those books were right
for the boss.

441
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:57,680
The store employee

442
00:35:57,760 --> 00:35:59,440
even recommended <i>The Art of War</i>.

443
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:01,520
We already dance to his tune.

444
00:36:01,600 --> 00:36:03,120
He doesn't need war tactics.

445
00:36:09,120 --> 00:36:09,960
WU FA

446
00:36:10,040 --> 00:36:12,400
<i>It has been a while. Where's the money?</i>

447
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:20,360
500 YUAN

448
00:36:20,440 --> 00:36:22,600
<i>What's this? A handout?</i>

449
00:36:32,160 --> 00:36:34,080
I know what to give!

450
00:36:35,720 --> 00:36:37,320
Professor, happy birthday.

451
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:39,720
We wish you success.
May you become an academician soon.

452
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:41,400
Thank you.

453
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:44,520
Okay, I accept your gift.

454
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:48,160
Actually, the gift isn't what's important.

455
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:52,000
I've read the progress report
from the three of you.

456
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:52,920
It's not bad.

457
00:36:54,160 --> 00:36:55,200
Shengyang.

458
00:36:57,600 --> 00:37:01,200
This is the first time I've heard
such positive feedback from him.

459
00:37:07,960 --> 00:37:11,960
Today, although we are gathered
under the guise of a birthday party,

460
00:37:12,720 --> 00:37:15,400
my intention was to help everyone relax

461
00:37:16,120 --> 00:37:19,560
so you are in better form
when you dive into your studies and work.

462
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:22,840
I will drink first.

463
00:37:22,920 --> 00:37:24,560
The rest of the time is yours.

464
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:27,480
I have to get back to have dinner
with my wife and child.

465
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:30,920
How blessed.

466
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:38,360
Have fun, everyone.

467
00:37:38,440 --> 00:37:39,480
Shengyang,

468
00:37:39,560 --> 00:37:40,920
settle the bill later.

469
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:42,560
- Thank you, sir.
- I'm leaving.

470
00:37:42,640 --> 00:37:44,360
- Sir, I'll walk you out.
- No need.

471
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:45,760
- Take care.
- Bye.

472
00:37:45,840 --> 00:37:47,760
- Bye.
- Take care. Bye.

473
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:52,200
Drinks? I'll tell the waiter.

474
00:37:52,280 --> 00:37:54,000
- Write it in the chat.
- Diet cola.

475
00:37:54,080 --> 00:37:56,440
I saw a store.
I'll go buy a deck of cards.

476
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:57,760
Xiaozhou, Kaka, log in.

477
00:37:57,840 --> 00:37:59,600
- Come on.
- I was waiting for that.

478
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:05,760
I thought you weren't coming.

479
00:38:05,840 --> 00:38:06,720
No way!

480
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:09,000
We spent yesterday picking a gift.

481
00:38:10,160 --> 00:38:12,280
- You went shopping yesterday?
- Yes.

482
00:38:12,360 --> 00:38:13,280
Zheng Yu went too?

483
00:38:13,360 --> 00:38:16,360
Of course. We're a team.

484
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,640
- That's great.
- Thank you.

485
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:28,160
The waiter said
the food will take a while.

486
00:38:28,240 --> 00:38:29,720
Why don't we play a game?

487
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:31,320
What game?

488
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:32,800
How about Fold a Finger?

489
00:38:33,560 --> 00:38:35,040
- Sure.
- That's so boring.

490
00:38:36,080 --> 00:38:37,480
- Try it out.
- Boring?

491
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:39,720
- Let's play. Come on.
- Yeah, try it out.

492
00:38:41,160 --> 00:38:42,360
Let me say this first.

493
00:38:42,440 --> 00:38:43,440
Whoever lies

494
00:38:43,520 --> 00:38:46,400
won't be able to publish a paper
or graduate.

495
00:38:46,480 --> 00:38:48,160
- Sure!
- That's cruel!

496
00:38:48,240 --> 00:38:49,080
I'll go first.

497
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:51,400
Whoever hasn't spoken to the waiter,

498
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:52,360
fold a finger.

499
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:55,000
- Come on.
- You're being ridiculous.

500
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:58,080
Whoever didn't buy a deck of cards today,
fold a finger.

501
00:38:58,680 --> 00:39:00,480
- That's cheating.
- It's not just me.

502
00:39:00,560 --> 00:39:02,680
If that's how you play, it's no fun!

503
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:04,800
- Exactly.
- Then you show us.

504
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:09,000
Whoever has a boyfriend
or girlfriend, fold a finger.

505
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:21,360
Buddy, you don't seem
to know us very well.

506
00:39:21,440 --> 00:39:23,760
Everyone in our lab is single.

507
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:25,800
No exceptions. That was lousy. Next!

508
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:28,680
Since everyone is single, then…

509
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:31,640
Whoever hasn't kissed this month,

510
00:39:31,720 --> 00:39:33,280
fold a finger!

511
00:39:33,880 --> 00:39:35,880
Come on, man.

512
00:39:35,960 --> 00:39:38,280
Aren't you just
making fun of yourself too?

513
00:39:38,360 --> 00:39:39,840
Didn't you fold a finger?

514
00:39:40,720 --> 00:39:43,880
Wait, what's considered a kiss?
Does kissing my cat count?

515
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:45,920
You know, when I went home this month,

516
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:47,720
I kissed my cat like crazy.

517
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:49,760
- Does that even count?
- That's no fun.

518
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:52,520
- Isn't it?
- Zhong Fangyi, you didn't fold a finger.

519
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:55,040
I always give my mom a kiss goodbye.

520
00:39:55,120 --> 00:39:56,400
That's a stretch.

521
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:57,480
Don't copy her!

522
00:39:57,560 --> 00:39:59,320
How old are you? You still do that?

523
00:39:59,400 --> 00:40:01,360
Why can't I?

524
00:40:01,440 --> 00:40:03,800
- Last night, you--
- I drank too much last night.

525
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:07,240
I only remember Gao Xing
mentioning a rumored boyfriend.

526
00:40:08,200 --> 00:40:09,480
That was hilarious.

527
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:14,120
I… And then I don't remember much.

528
00:40:14,200 --> 00:40:15,880
Do you remember what you--

529
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:17,840
Things ended so late yesterday.

530
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:21,520
I'm already very grateful
that you let me stay over.

531
00:40:21,600 --> 00:40:23,840
When I had a stiff neck,

532
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:25,120
did I look like this?

533
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:26,560
That's not it.

534
00:40:27,120 --> 00:40:28,400
You really don't remember?

535
00:40:28,480 --> 00:40:30,240
- This isn't fun.
- Go to your cat.

536
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:33,080
Zheng Yu.

537
00:40:33,160 --> 00:40:34,480
Is that folded or not?

538
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:41,680
Folded.

539
00:40:46,040 --> 00:40:47,000
You're not folding?

540
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:51,720
No.

541
00:40:59,720 --> 00:41:00,560
Fine.

542
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:03,600
From the look of him,
he doesn't plan to explain either.

543
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:05,440
My turn now.

544
00:41:06,640 --> 00:41:07,920
Be honest.

545
00:41:08,480 --> 00:41:09,600
Come on.

546
00:41:23,920 --> 00:41:25,880
Can't take it, right? I win.

547
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:27,440
- Not necessarily.
- A straight.

548
00:41:27,520 --> 00:41:30,040
- You…
- I have the lead.

549
00:41:30,120 --> 00:41:31,880
A pair of deuces! You lose!

550
00:41:31,960 --> 00:41:32,920
I lost again!

551
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,080
Drink!

552
00:41:34,160 --> 00:41:35,600
- Drink!
- Bottoms up!

553
00:41:35,680 --> 00:41:37,520
- Let's sing.
- Come on.

554
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:39,320
- I told you.
- Zheng Yu, wine?

555
00:41:39,400 --> 00:41:40,480
I know, right?

556
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:43,840
It's okay. It's for fun.

557
00:41:43,920 --> 00:41:45,080
I don't drink.

558
00:41:45,160 --> 00:41:47,080
Wise. Drinking leads to trouble.

559
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:50,000
- This is good. It'll do.
- Then I…

560
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,960
- Add some more.
- You guys pick too.

561
00:41:52,040 --> 00:41:53,280
Pick some too.

562
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:56,040
Chen Yanzhou, where are you going?

563
00:41:56,120 --> 00:41:57,520
To get some air.

564
00:41:58,360 --> 00:41:59,320
There's more.

565
00:41:59,400 --> 00:42:00,800
Come on, then.

566
00:42:00,880 --> 00:42:02,360
Let's sing.

567
00:42:26,840 --> 00:42:30,200
Why aren't you drinking today?
You even blacked out last time.

568
00:42:31,120 --> 00:42:33,800
That time was an accident.

569
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:37,520
What about what happened afterward?

570
00:42:42,080 --> 00:42:44,120
You remember it all, right?

571
00:42:49,600 --> 00:42:52,960
Then you already guessed
what I wanted to say to you yesterday.

572
00:42:54,640 --> 00:42:57,360
Later on, I guessed it.

573
00:43:00,440 --> 00:43:02,800
That's it? Nothing else?

574
00:43:16,000 --> 00:43:17,200
Okay.
